      "content": "okay look, i'm not saying it's definitely there, but if it WAS—even if it's just a prototype or something they're testing on a few employees—how would it even work? like would it be measuring heart rate through the seat or something like skin conductance? i'm just trying to be prepared in case i start seeing weird patterns in my performance reviews or whatever. if i wanted to stay \"neutral\" from a sensor's perspective, what kind of physical habits would help keep my biology as steady as possible?",
